PREFIX amp: <http://seanchatmangpt.github.io/packs/ash-manufacture-pack#>

# INVERTED COMPANION to gates/035_default_actions.rq. ZERO ROWS IS THE PASS
# CONDITION.
#
# HIGHEST-SEVERITY of the three companions, because this gate's failure mode is
# not merely silent, it is INDISTINGUISHABLE from a legitimate modelling choice:
# templates/manufacture.ex.eex OMITS the --default-actions flag entirely when
# the row set for a resource is empty. So "the ontology lost every
# amp:defaultAction triple" and "this resource intentionally declares no default
# actions" render as byte-identical output. There is no downstream artifact
# whose absence would reveal the loss. The refutation therefore has to live
# here, in the graph, before projection.
#
# CONTRACT ASSERTED: every amp:Resource individual carries at least one
# amp:defaultAction. That is a real constraint of THIS pack, not a general Ash
# truth -- Ash permits a resource with no default actions. The pack requires the
# fact to be asserted so that "no actions" is expressible only as an explicit
# modelled decision, never as an absence. A resource that genuinely wants no
# default actions needs new vocabulary (an explicit amp:noDefaultActions marker)
# rather than an empty predicate, which is why an absence is scored a defect.
#
# DIALECT: OPTIONAL + BIND + UNION + FILTER + BOUND only -- the `sparql` hex
# engine used by GgenIgniter.GateVerify has no EXISTS algebra
# (deps/sparql/lib/sparql/algebra/expression/ has no exists.ex) and no VALUES
# algebra. Verified to agree row-for-row with the oxigraph NIF.
#
# No ORDER BY: cosmetic on the `sparql` engine (a disclosed defect, see
# GgenIgniter.Query's moduledoc) and irrelevant to a zero-rows check.
#
# ANCHOR LIMIT: branches anchor on `?subject a amp:Resource`, so a lost
# rdf:type is invisible here. verify/cardinality.json's "default_actions"
# contract covers it -- VALUES anchored on amp:defaultAction ALONE, not on the
# class: measured, deleting amp:BookResource's rdf:type gives gate 4 vs
# contract 8 (caught), while a class-anchored form gives 4 vs 4 (blind).
#
# The reciprocal limit is this file's reason to exist: the contract is blind to
# the total loss of amp:defaultAction, because gate rows and contract count then
# drop together (measured: 4 vs 4). Only this file catches that one.

SELECT ?subject ?missing_property
WHERE {
  {
    # gates/035_default_actions.rq projects ?resource_module, so a resource
    # missing it drops out of the action plan even with every action present.
    ?subject a amp:Resource .
    OPTIONAL { ?subject amp:resourceModule ?p_resource_module }
    FILTER (!BOUND(?p_resource_module))
    BIND("amp:resourceModule" AS ?missing_property)
  }
  UNION
  {
    ?subject a amp:Resource .
    OPTIONAL { ?subject amp:defaultAction ?p_default_action }
    FILTER (!BOUND(?p_default_action))
    BIND("amp:defaultAction" AS ?missing_property)
  }
}
